# Commit as you go

When making changes in this repository:

- **Commit modularly while working**, not only at the end of a multi-step task.
- After each coherent unit of work (e.g. one UI fix, one feature, one data update), stage and commit that unit before moving on.
- Prefer several focused commits over one large dump.
- Follow the existing git safety protocol (status/diff/log, HEREDOC messages, no force-push, no amend unless explicitly requested).
- If the user says "commit as you go" or similar, treat it as a standing instruction for the session and for future work in this repo.
